Inspect and manage directory
authorizations and .cronrc
configurations

Usage:
  cron-person dir [flags] [command]

Available Commands:
├─ allow [path]
│      Authorize .cronrc in the
│      specified directory
├─ check [path]
│      Validate syntax and parseability
│      of a .cronrc file
├─ deny [path]
│      Revoke authorization for the
│      specified directory
╰─ status [path]
       Show status and tasks for a
       specific directory

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for dir

Global Flags:
      --config string
        Path to custom configuration
        file (default:
        $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/cron-person/config.json)
      --store string
        Path to custom authorization
        state file (default:
        $XDG_STATE_HOME/cron-person/allowed.json)

Use "cron-person dir [command] --help"
for more information about a command.
